==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|es|Tierra del Fuego|lit=Land of Fire|withtext=1}}, reportedly named so by {{w|Ferdinand Magellan}} after the many fires lit up by the local population.

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia|dab=Tierra del Fuego (disambiguation)|Tierra del Fuego}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/tɪˌɛːɹə dɛl ˈfweɪɡəʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/tiˌɛɹə dɛl ˈfweɪɡoʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪɡəʊ|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=Tierra del Fuego}}

# {{def|An island at the southern tip of [[South America]], divided between [[Chile]] and [[Argentina]].}}
# {{def|The [[archipelago]] consisting of this island and a number of smaller surrounding islands.}}
#: {{syn|en|Fireland|q1=archaic}}
# {{place|en|province|c/Argentina|capital=[[Ushuaia]]}}
# {{place|en|province|c/Chile|capital=[[Porvenir]]}}

